WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.666
Welcome to the Genmab Website Design System Designer tutorial.

00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:08.033
This video is for designers creating website experiences for Genmab.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.766
Use of the design system is a required part of the website

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:13.366
design process for all agency partners.

00:00:13.366 --> 00:00:16.000
In this video, we'll walk through how to access the design

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.200
system, understand and leverage its various features,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.433
how to move from design to development, plus where to go for support.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.100
To get the latest version of the website design kit.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.033
Go to helix and navigate to Channel Guidance,

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.433
then websites.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.000
Website design system,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.700
website design kit

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.300
and finally design Kit.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.633
Click the button to open the file in view only mode.

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:49.566
From there, use the dropdown menu to duplicate it to your drafts.

00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:52.566
This creates a new file with all permissions removed

00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:57.000
so you can edit, rename, save, and move it wherever you like.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.400
Finally, to make sure you have the latest version, click this button.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.700
It will link to the current file or newer version if one is available.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:08.633
Now that you have created your own

00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:12.966
copy of the design kit file, let's take a look at what's inside.

00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:16.233
Starting with the left sidebar, the Pages and Layers panel,

00:01:16.233 --> 00:01:18.100
we have the Getting Started page,

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.966
which contains an overview of the content along with direct

00:01:20.966 --> 00:01:24.100
links to specific pages within the kit.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.733
Next is the foundations page covering design, kit, essentials, color

00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:32.100
and theme modes, typography and columns.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.633
The presets page contains desktop, tablet and mobile page frames

00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:40.500
based on website type, with navigation and theme modes already applied.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.366
The component overview page provides an at a glance listing

00:01:43.366 --> 00:01:48.233
of all components, with links to the component reference pages.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:50.833
The next set of pages cover each component in detail,

00:01:50.833 --> 00:01:54.933
including properties and variants, as well as color and font options.

00:01:54.933 --> 00:02:00.066
And finally, the changelog page lists version and update details.

00:02:00.066 --> 00:02:03.666
Moving over to the right sidebar, the Properties and Inspector panel

00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:08.500
you will find available text styles, effects and layout guides.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.666
Theme modes included in this version of the design

00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:14.166
kit can be viewed in the variables panel.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.100
Keep in mind that the right sidebar is contextual

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.100
and will change depending on what is selected on the canvas.

00:02:26.466 --> 00:02:27.600
The first step in creating

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.333
a website is choosing a preset based on website type.

00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:34.033
There are three preset types. Brand.

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:38.100
Brand with indication selector and Genmab Corporate.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:43.000
This version of the design kit also includes a MyNavCare preset.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.133
Each preset includes desktop,

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.800
tablet, and mobile page frames with an applied

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.600
theme mode along with header, footer, and navigation flows.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.400
There are two sub navigation options to choose from.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.633
A full width menu and dropdown menu.

00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:59.933
The page frames also have Auto Layout applied

00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:03.333
to support drag and drop page creation.

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:06.333
For this tutorial, we will use the BrandMab preset.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.833
Once you have selected a preset, it's

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.566
time to think about file structure

00:03:14.566 --> 00:03:17.500
and where the website design will live.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.133
As you become familiar with the kit and components,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.800
you'll find the workflow that works best for you.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:23.700
In this tutorial,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.133
we'll share some preferred methods

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.700
for structuring the file and adding components.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.433
Keep in mind,

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:29.666
unless the kit is published

00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:32.133
within your organization as a design library,

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.866
the website design will need to remain

00:03:33.866 --> 00:03:36.900
in this file to access components locally.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.933
Let's begin by renaming the design kit.

00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:43.900
A clean version of

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.900
the original design kit can be used for the next project,

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.900
or related deliverables can be added to this file.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.200
Now let's copy and paste the preset to a new page

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.666
and give it a name.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.066
Move the pages from the preset

00:04:05.066 --> 00:04:08.066
frame onto the canvas and rename.

00:04:39.366 --> 00:04:40.400
For the navigation.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.400
Create a separate frame showing all expanded views.

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:47.333
Now we're ready to start adding components.

00:04:51.733 --> 00:04:52.733
Adding components to

00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:55.866
the page is simple and can be done in a couple of ways.

00:04:55.866 --> 00:04:59.100
Starting with the desktop page, let's add a hero.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:02.700
We can drag the component directly from the assets panel onto the page.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.100
Positioning the cursor

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.100
where we would like it to appear in the stacking order.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.966
Or we can select a component

00:05:09.966 --> 00:05:13.133
already in the page frame and use the swap instance function.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.800
Duplicating components within the auto layout frame

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:26.400
and using swap instance is one of the fastest ways to add components.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.400
while designing the page.

00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:34.133
If we configure the desktop component first

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.200
with the desired variant properties and content,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.333
we can then use copy and paste to replace

00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:41.533
across the tablet and mobile pages.

00:05:41.533 --> 00:05:45.500
Update the device variants and only configure the component once.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.500
Reducing errors and speeding up development.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.633
Finally, it's worth mentioning that

00:06:06.633 --> 00:06:07.833
because all components

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.900
are designed at desktop, tablet, and mobile widths,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.800
keeping the page frame auto layout set to top center

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.833
with horizontal and vertical hug enabled is recommended.

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.700
Now that we've added components to the page, let's take a closer

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.000
look at how they work.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.800
The component library

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.033
consists of two main types based components—

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:35.566
Single reusable elements like buttons, containers, and text,

00:06:35.566 --> 00:06:36.833
and component groups

00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:42.300
or patterns such as navigation bars, hero sections, and card layouts.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.366
Components are listed

00:06:43.366 --> 00:06:45.066
alphabetically in the Assets Panel,

00:06:45.066 --> 00:06:47.733
and can be viewed in either grid or list view.

00:06:48.866 --> 00:06:51.600
Make sure show subfolders is selected.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:52.933
This keeps component atoms

00:06:52.933 --> 00:06:55.933
grouped inside folders and out of the way for easier browsing.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.133
When designing a website, we should always use instances

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:01.400
of these pre-built patterns

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.233
and configure them

00:07:02.233 --> 00:07:05.266
using the available variants, properties and color options.

00:07:05.966 --> 00:07:08.966
Detaching components is not recommended or supported,

00:07:08.966 --> 00:07:11.966
except in a few cases covered later in the tutorial.

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:15.366
Keeping components connected is important

00:07:15.366 --> 00:07:18.366
because detached instances no longer receive updates

00:07:18.366 --> 00:07:21.633
or have access to component properties and variants.

00:07:21.633 --> 00:07:23.233
Connected components help maintain

00:07:23.233 --> 00:07:26.233
consistency, reduce errors, and speeds up development.

00:07:27.266 --> 00:07:29.466
Finally, while this design system does

00:07:29.466 --> 00:07:31.300
support atomic design through custom

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.566
layouts built with base components, it should be used sparingly

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.666
since it requires more time for both design and development.

00:07:42.233 --> 00:07:45.000
Variants and properties make components more flexible

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.900
and reusable while maintaining consistency across the design system.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.633
An easy way to explore component

00:07:50.633 --> 00:07:53.800
variants and properties is in the details panel.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.433
Let's take a look at the hero component.

00:07:56.433 --> 00:07:58.800
Variants are different versions of a component grouped

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.600
within the same component set.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:04.333
They allow you to switch between options such as device type, style,

00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:07.333
image position, and more without creating separate components.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.000
Properties are customizable settings within a component that allow you

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:12.933
to change content,

00:08:12.933 --> 00:08:16.833
behavior, or visibility without detaching the component.

00:08:16.833 --> 00:08:17.800
Nested properties

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:18.600
become available

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.566
when a base component is placed inside a larger component,

00:08:21.566 --> 00:08:24.466
such as a button inside a hero.

00:08:24.466 --> 00:08:27.233
You can also preview the different theme modes.

00:08:27.233 --> 00:08:30.300
The design kit also includes a reference page for each component,

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:33.866
showing the available variants, properties, and color options.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.200
The main component is included for publishing purposes only

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.400
and should never be edited.

00:08:42.466 --> 00:08:43.900
All components have default

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:47.800
color and font styles applied as defined by the theme modes.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:51.166
Additional options can be applied to an instance using the Properties

00:08:51.166 --> 00:08:52.600
and Inspector panel.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.900
Let's take a look at the color bar card component and see how.

00:08:58.333 --> 00:09:01.200
The first step is to go to the component reference page.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.500
Apply the mode you're working in and review the available options.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:08.400
BrandMab is the default theme mode for this version of the design kit.

00:09:09.066 --> 00:09:12.600
Here you can see the available options six background colors,

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.600
six bar colors, and the ability to change the font size and style

00:09:18.666 --> 00:09:20.133
To apply a different color,

00:09:20.133 --> 00:09:24.033
select the instance Open Selection colors and choose a new color

00:09:24.033 --> 00:09:27.033
that corresponds to the color variable you want to change.

00:09:28.433 --> 00:09:30.366
To change a font size or style,

00:09:30.366 --> 00:09:34.333
select the text layer and apply the new size and or style.

00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:37.766
Headline sizes are specific to desktop, tablet, and mobile.

00:09:37.766 --> 00:09:41.366
While body sizes are shared across all three.

00:09:41.366 --> 00:09:44.266
To add an effect such as the container drop shadow,

00:09:44.266 --> 00:09:47.966
select a container instance and choose the effects style.

00:09:47.966 --> 00:09:50.733
Keep in mind that color options and font customization

00:09:50.733 --> 00:09:54.000
vary by component, so be sure to check the reference pages before

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.266
making any changes.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.100
Let's take a look at how images work within the design system.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.566
Images exist both as base components and as nested components

00:10:05.566 --> 00:10:09.333
within larger patterns like heros, content blocks and cards.

00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:13.166
The base component settings default to square corners,

00:10:13.166 --> 00:10:16.800
image position top center, and captions turned on.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.166
Placeholder graphics are included that can be used for wireframing,

00:10:20.166 --> 00:10:22.500
deleted or left hidden in the instance.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.500
For now, let's turn off the caption.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:30.600
Corners,

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.566
which are defined by the active theme mode

00:10:32.566 --> 00:10:35.200
can be set to square or radius.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.466
Image position defines how the image crops

00:10:37.466 --> 00:10:41.266
as the viewport gets smaller and components become narrower.

00:10:41.266 --> 00:10:42.700
Always choose the image position

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.233
variant before applying the image fill.

00:10:45.233 --> 00:10:47.833
Image position top center works best for centered

00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:52.200
focal points, cropping the left and right sides equally.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.400
To accurately represent this in your design.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:58.500
Select the image layer, apply an image fill and set it to fill.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.933
This automatically positions

00:10:59.933 --> 00:11:04.166
the image and only needs to be done once in the desktop variant.

00:11:04.166 --> 00:11:06.566
Image positions top left and top right,

00:11:06.566 --> 00:11:09.666
Pin the image to one side as the viewport narrows.

00:11:09.666 --> 00:11:12.366
Cropping only one side of the image

00:11:12.366 --> 00:11:14.533
to accurately represent this in your design.

00:11:14.533 --> 00:11:18.800
Select the image layer, apply an image fill, set it to fill,

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.233
then switch to crop and manually reposition

00:11:21.233 --> 00:11:24.466
the image by sliding it left or right.

00:11:24.466 --> 00:11:28.166
This will need to be done for desktop, tablet and mobile.

00:11:28.166 --> 00:11:31.066
An additional image fill option can be found in components

00:11:31.066 --> 00:11:32.833
with background image variants.

00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:33.966
This Gradient Overlay

00:11:33.966 --> 00:11:37.900
option helps maintain contrast and improves text readability.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:41.100
You can adjust the number of stops, direction, colors, and opacity.

00:11:41.766 --> 00:11:46.366
Gradient overlays are added by the builder using standard CSS gradients

00:11:46.366 --> 00:11:49.100
and should not be included in the exported image.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.533
Also, for these variants, the image position

00:11:51.533 --> 00:11:54.566
will need to be manually annotated in the file.

00:11:54.566 --> 00:11:57.800
Finally, images can be exported directly from Figma

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.966
or an image editing application.

00:11:59.966 --> 00:12:00.633
Both methods

00:12:00.633 --> 00:12:03.166
require specific sizing and cropping approaches

00:12:03.166 --> 00:12:05.900
depending on the image position you've selected.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:09.033
As a general rule, size your image to match the height

00:12:09.033 --> 00:12:12.300
and width of the desktop image at 2x resolution.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:15.233
We recommend using the WebP file format.

00:12:15.233 --> 00:12:18.500
SVG images are recommended for vector graphics.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.366
Note that the hero component requires

00:12:20.366 --> 00:12:22.633
 a mobile specific crop and export.